    {
      "id": "entity-city-council-discussion-2019-05-14-new-officers",
      "type": "folder",
      "label": "Swearing-in of four police officers",
      "anchor": "discussion-2019-05-14-new-officers",
      "contents": [
        {
          "type": "formatted-text",
          "preserve-paragraphs": true,
          "segments": [
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Context written for this site: "
            },
            {
              "text": "Mayor Frost commented on four newly sworn American Fork police officers and Chief Falslev’s role in recruiting them."
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Relevant discussion from the official meeting minutes: "
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\nMayor Frost reported he was grateful to work with great people who are making American Fork great. He said the staff and Council were great people. He stated that he was pleased about the swearing in of four new officers to the American Fork Police Department. He paid tribute to Chief Falslev. He stated that 3 of the 4 recruits were attracted to American Fork because they wanted to work with Chief Falslev.\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "link",
              "text": "View minutes, page 4",
              "url": "/records/american-fork-city/city-council-session-minutes/american-fork-city-council-regular-session-minutes-2019-05-14.pdf#page=4"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "entity-city-council-discussion-2019-05-14-patrol-car-crash",
      "type": "folder",
      "label": "Police patrol-car crash",
      "anchor": "discussion-2019-05-14-patrol-car-crash",
      "contents": [
        {
          "type": "formatted-text",
          "preserve-paragraphs": true,
          "segments": [
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Context written for this site: "
            },
            {
              "text": "Council Member Carroll reported an accident involving a stopped patrol car."
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Relevant discussion from the official meeting minutes: "
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\nCouncil Member Carroll explained this included one additional item sent out. She shared a story about an accident that occurred a few days ago involving one of the police officers where the officer was at a stop sign when a car turned the corner and hit the patrol car head on. Luckily no one was seriously injured.\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "link",
              "text": "View minutes, page 4",
              "url": "/records/american-fork-city/city-council-session-minutes/american-fork-city-council-regular-session-minutes-2019-05-14.pdf#page=4"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "entity-city-council-discussion-2019-05-14-short-term-rental-enforcement",
      "type": "folder",
      "label": "Short-term-rental enforcement",
      "anchor": "discussion-2019-05-14-short-term-rental-enforcement",
      "contents": [
        {
          "type": "formatted-text",
          "preserve-paragraphs": true,
          "segments": [
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Context written for this site: "
            },
            {
              "text": "Council Members Taylor and Barnes discussed police and code-enforcement implications while considering a short-term-rental ordinance."
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "bold",
              "text": "Relevant discussion from the official meeting minutes: "
            },
            {
              "text": "\n\nCouncil Member Taylor commented the protection of the quality of life was the Council’s job. He noted there was not enough money to hire enough enforcement officers. He said he agreed with what had been discussed and thought they needed to rewrite the ordinance. They needed better enforcement and restrictions before they passed the ordinance.\n\nCouncil member Taylor said they needed to decide where they permitted short-term rentals. Council Member Shelton and Christensen agreed.\n\nCouncil Member Barnes commented he wanted to support personal property rights. He noted this issue affected people’s property rights and neighbors. He said they needed to investigate how this would affect the residents and the police force. He noted he had been called by residents that had issues. He said the police needed to be contacted when there were problems. He said they needed to create an ordinance to get experience.\n\n"
            },
            {
              "format": "link",
              "text": "View minutes, page 6",
              "url": "/records/american-fork-city/city-council-session-minutes/american-fork-city-council-regular-session-minutes-2019-05-14.pdf#page=6"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
